ng of the word\n\nJatukarnya: Jatukarnya; cha-tatha; tat-shishyah: Shakalya's disciple; sa-niruktam: to explain difficult words; with the collection of words; swa-samhitam: the collected one that has been obtained; balak-pail-jabal-virajebhyah: balak, pail, jabal\nAnd viraj; dadau: gave; munih: the sage. The sage Jatukarnya was also a disciple of Shakalya. He divided the Samhita received from Shakalya into three\ndivisions, and added a fourth section to it, the Vedic vocabulary (Nirukta). He taught one division each from these four parts to his four disciples—Balak, Second Pail,\nJabal and Viraj."
